1
00:00:01,509 --> 00:00:06,780
Imagine in your organization a couple of services run on Google Cloud,

2
00:00:06,989 --> 00:00:12,869
some of them on GKE, some of them are legacy services which are on‑prem,

3
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:19,270
and your CTO wants to deploy everything faster without breaking the production.

4
00:00:19,549 --> 00:00:23,729
Now how do you build the CI/CD system that works across GCP

5
00:00:24,995 --> 00:00:28,934
hybrid environment and maybe even multiple cloud? That's

6
00:00:28,934 --> 00:00:29,864
what we're going to see here.

7
00:00:30,975 --> 00:00:35,215
Before that, first understand what CI/CD really is.

8
00:00:35,455 --> 00:00:39,834
CI/CD is more than just running tests and deploying code.

9
00:00:40,115 --> 00:00:45,095
Google defines it as a fully automated path from commit to

10
00:00:45,095 --> 00:00:47,974
production with guardrails for safety.

11
00:00:48,205 --> 00:00:53,779
A modern CI/CD pipeline includes the continuous integration,

12
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:59,690
continuous delivery that moves the artifact across environments automatically,

13
00:00:59,690 --> 00:01:04,000
and it also has the continuous deployment that fully

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,779
automates the deployment into the production.

15
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:13,160
You can think of CI as creation and validation and CD as promotion and release.

16
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,324
Artifact Registry is the single source of truth.

17
00:01:16,565 --> 00:01:20,654
All build outputs like containers, Maven packages,

18
00:01:20,934 --> 00:01:25,144
node modules, Terraform modules go into the Artifact Registry.

19
00:01:25,415 --> 00:01:28,775
Google recommends Artifact Registry because it

20
00:01:28,775 --> 00:01:30,834
supports the multi‑region replication.

21
00:01:31,014 --> 00:01:34,415
It integrates with the Cloud Build and Cloud Deploy.

22
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:38,464
It enforces the IAM at the repository level,

23
00:01:38,614 --> 00:01:42,029
and It logs everything for your audit,

24
00:01:42,269 --> 00:01:45,910
so no more mixing artifacts in the random places.

25
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:51,760
The Cloud Build is your CI engine that handles and runs your unit test,

26
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:55,980
your linting, your container builds, your security scans,

27
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:59,389
your SBOM generation, and preview deployments.

28
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:04,739
Cloud Build is serverless, so it scales beautifully during busy times.

29
00:02:04,919 --> 00:02:10,029
Cloud Deploy handles the promotion of artifacts through your dev,

30
00:02:10,389 --> 00:02:16,130
staging, and prod. Cloud Deploy pipeline supports canary rollouts,

31
00:02:16,389 --> 00:02:18,899
blue‑green deployments, manual approvals,

32
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:24,270
your scaffold integration, rollbacks, and your multi‑service orchestration.

33
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:28,649
Cloud Deploy stores release history, approvals,

34
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:33,389
and rollbacks, extremely important for compliance‑heavy industries.

35
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:38,705
Cloud Deploy natively integrates with customize for environment

36
00:02:38,705 --> 00:02:42,824
overlays and scaffold for build and deploy workflows.

37
00:02:42,955 --> 00:02:47,595
This is how you avoid duplicating the YAML across environment.

38
00:02:47,794 --> 00:02:53,464
Each environment gets its own small patch, clean and elegant.

39
00:02:53,804 --> 00:02:57,205
Now let's expand to the hybrid environment where

40
00:02:57,434 --> 00:02:59,744
some of the services in the GCP,

41
00:03:00,074 --> 00:03:05,110
some of them in the on‑prem and some are still legacy applications.

42
00:03:05,169 --> 00:03:09,169
This is common in the banking, telecom, and healthcare retail.

43
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:13,059
Now we need a pipeline that must deploy everywhere.

44
00:03:13,339 --> 00:03:15,320
This can be done in multiple ways.

45
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:18,949
The first one would be the Cloud Build builds.

46
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:23,389
Cloud Build can push artifacts to on‑prem Kubernetes,

47
00:03:23,669 --> 00:03:24,690
Anthos clusters,

48
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:30,610
bare metal GKE, virtual machines, and legacy deployment systems.

49
00:03:30,610 --> 00:03:35,940
Because Cloud Build uses an extensive builder model, you can run any

50
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:39,380
script needed to deploy to private environments.

51
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:44,429
Another option is Anthos configuration management with GitOps.

52
00:03:44,529 --> 00:03:48,779
Hybrid pipeline often use a Git as the truth model.

53
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:56,389
Cloud Build publishes and Anthos config management syncs it to on‑prem GKE,

54
00:03:56,630 --> 00:03:59,929
Cloud GKE, and the edge clusters.

55
00:04:00,089 --> 00:04:04,350
Another option is secure VPN or interconnected deployment.

56
00:04:04,589 --> 00:04:09,869
Cloud Build can reach private clusters using Cloud VPN,

57
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:12,690
Cloud Interconnect, and authorized networks.

58
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:16,510
This is common for sensitive regulated workloads.

59
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:19,548
Some companies deploy to the multi‑cloud,

60
00:04:19,769 --> 00:04:24,630
where it could be GCP and AWS, GCP and Azure,

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,890
or maybe GCP and on‑prem.

62
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:30,100
Here the typical pipeline would be Cloud Build perform,

63
00:04:30,239 --> 00:04:34,119
build, and security scans, artifacts stored in Artifact Registry.

64
00:04:34,769 --> 00:04:37,489
Cloud Deploy handles GCP deployments.

65
00:04:37,779 --> 00:04:43,709
GitHub Action or GitLab CI deploys to AWS or Azure,

66
00:04:43,899 --> 00:04:47,160
and monitoring centralized in the Google Cloud monitoring.

67
00:04:47,459 --> 00:04:51,559
Multi‑cloud CI/CD is mostly about the standardization,

68
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,720
which has the same build system,

69
00:04:53,899 --> 00:04:58,440
same configuration model and separate delivery engines per cloud.

70
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,859
This keeps complexity manageable.

71
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:06,239
So that's the foundation of designing a modern CI/CD system for Google Cloud.
